{"cells":[{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"e01d2f96","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"db07df61-043a-4b18-9b1d-730c9a6f59b2","_uuid":"2558957b-b65d-40c4-9c47-f8b1157baa52","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T04:18:42.706952Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T04:18:42.706657Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.931996Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.931023Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":8.233035,"end_time":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.933937+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T04:18:42.700902+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["\"\"\"\n","Stage 1: Standalone Tabular LightGBM Baseline (Audit-Hardened Edition, v2)\n","=========================================================================\n","Purpose\n","-------\n","Produce (a) an honest, temporally-causal tabular benchmark for IEEE-CIS fraud\n","detection, and (b) a leakage-free `stage1_prob` representation consumable by a\n","downstream graph / joint model WITHOUT re-introducing look-ahead bias.\n","\n","What changed vs. v1 (and why)\n","-----------------------------\n"," 1. EVALUATION and FEATURE-GENERATION are now separate passes with different\n","    rules. v1 conflated them: the embargo (an evaluation-integrity device) was\n","    silently destroying ~3% of OOF coverage in Blocks 2-4, and the sealed OOT\n","    block received no score at all (0% coverage), which makes the artifact\n","    unusable for Stage-2 inference on Block 5.\n"," 2. Block 1 OOF now uses an expanding chronological sub-fold scheme\n","    (K slices, train-on-past -> score-next) instead of a single half-split.\n","    Coverage rises from 50% -> (K-1)/K (75% at K=4) and the retained slice is\n","    explicitly labelled rather than silently NaN.\n"," 3. Sub-fold models select their own boosting rounds via their own inner\n","    early-stopping split. v1 imported `mean(best_iterations)` from folds that\n","    had themselves trained on Block 1 - an arbitrary, never-validated schedule\n","    with mild hyperparameter circularity.\n"," 4. Final OOT scorer: a frozen model fit on Blocks 1-4 scores Block 5. The\n","    Block 5 TARGET is never read; enforced by assertion, not by convention.\n"," 5. Probability calibration (isotonic, fit strictly on the inner-stopping\n","    split) is now fit and applied. v1 measured ECE/Brier but never acted on\n","    them, so `stage1_oof_prob` was a good ranker and a mediocre probability.\n"," 6. Explicit missingness policy: `stage1_oof_missing` flag + documented prior\n","    fill, so Stage-2 cannot silently interpret NaN->0 as \"certainly legitimate\".\n"," 7. Hard causality assertions on EVERY train->score pair (train_max_dt <=\n","    score_min_dt) and a global assertion that no OOT row ever enters training.\n"," 8. Entity-overlap audit (card / device seen-rate between train and score\n","    windows) to contextualise AP; plus first-seen vs seen-before cohort AP.\n"," 9. Feature-importance stability: per-fold gain/split importance exported, with\n","    cross-fold Spearman rank correlation. Stable importance is evidence the\n","    model learns transferable structure rather than fold-specific noise.\n","10. LightGBM bug fix: `subsample=0.8` was INACTIVE in v1 because\n","    `bagging_freq` defaulted to 0. Row subsampling never actually happened.\n","11. Determinism flags (`deterministic`, `force_row_wise`, explicit sub-seeds).\n","12. ECE reported with both equal-width and equal-frequency (quantile) bins;\n","    on a ~3.5% prevalence problem equal-width ECE is dominated by the near-zero\n","    bin and flatters the model.\n","\n","Protocol invariants (unchanged from v1, retained deliberately)\n","--------------------------------------------------------------\n","  - Equal-row deterministic chronological blocks; Blocks 1-4 dev, Block 5 OOT.\n","  - 1-day boundary embargo on REPORTED validation metrics.\n","  - Inner-split early stopping (never the reported validation block).\n","  - Cost-sensitive Bayes alert rule: p* = (C_rev + C_fric) / (Amt + C_fric).\n","  - Reference rungs (Random, Amount-only) with paired bootstrap CIs.\n","\"\"\"\n","\n","from __future__ import annotations\n","\n","import gc\n","import hashlib\n","import json\n","import os\n","import warnings\n","from datetime import datetime, timezone\n","\n","import lightgbm as lgb\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","from sklearn.isotonic import IsotonicRegression\n","from sklearn.metrics import average_precision_score, roc_auc_score\n","\n","warnings.simplefilter(\"default\")\n","warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=UserWarning, module=\"lightgbm\")\n","warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\",\n","    category=DeprecationWarning,\n","    message=r\"datetime\\.datetime\\.utcnow\\(\\) is deprecated.*\",\n",")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"bca3c88f","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"8272ba7f-2256-4a9e-a00b-db63db9c3b9b","_uuid":"e9445c12-4fa9-4d08-8462-6285cb0608bd","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.94151Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.94093Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.949552Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.948805Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.01406,"end_time":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.951043+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.936983+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 1. Configuration and Constants\n","# ==============================================================================\n","CONFIG = {\n","    # --- Reproducibility & Schema ---\n","    \"SEED\": 42,\n","    \"TIME_COLUMN\": \"TransactionDT\",\n","    \"TARGET_COLUMN\": \"isFraud\",\n","    \"ID_COLUMN\": \"TransactionID\",\n","    \"AMOUNT_COLUMN\": \"TransactionAmt\",\n","\n","    # --- Temporal Split & Embargo Protocol ---\n","    \"N_BLOCKS\": 5,\n","    \"DEV_BLOCKS\": [1, 2, 3, 4],\n","    \"OOT_BLOCK\": 5,                  # Sealed holdout: scored, never trained on\n","    \"SECONDS_PER_DAY\": 86_400,\n","    \"EMBARGO_SECONDS\": 86_400,       # Applied to EVALUATION only (see note below)\n","\n","    # NOTE ON EMBARGO SEMANTICS\n","    # The embargo removes optimistic bias from *reported* metrics by discarding\n","    # validation rows temporally adjacent to the training edge. It is NOT a\n","    # causality device - causality is guaranteed by train_max_dt <= score_min_dt.\n","    # For feature generation we therefore score the full block (embargo off) so\n","    # Stage-2 gets complete coverage, exactly as a deployed model retrained\n","    # yesterday would score today's traffic.\n","    \"EMBARGO_IN_FEATURE_PASS\": False,\n","\n","    # --- Early Stopping & Validation Integrity ---\n","    \"INNER_VAL_FRAC\": 0.20,          # Final 20% of the training window stops boosting\n","    \"MIN_STOP_ROWS\": 5_000,          # Below this, early stopping is unreliable\n","    \"MIN_STOP_POSITIVES\": 50,        # AP-based stopping needs enough positives\n","\n","    # --- Block 1 OOF sub-fold scheme ---\n","    \"B1_SUBFOLDS\": 4,                # Expanding slices -> (K-1)/K coverage\n","\n","    # --- Boosting-round rule for models that cannot early-stop ---\n","    \"FINAL_ROUNDS_RULE\": \"median\",   # {\"median\", \"last\", \"mean\"}\n","\n","    # --- Calibration ---\n","    \"CALIBRATION\": \"isotonic\",       # {\"isotonic\", \"none\"}\n","    \"EXPORT_CALIBRATED_OOF\": True,\n","\n","    # --- Cost Model (Bayes-Optimal Decision Boundary) ---\n","    # Alert iff  p*Amt  >  C_rev + (1-p)*C_fric   <=>   p > (C_rev+C_fric)/(Amt+C_fric)\n","    \"C_REVIEW\": 10.0,\n","    \"C_FRICTION\": 25.0,\n","\n","    # --- Operational Triage & Bootstrap Benchmarks ---\n","    \"INVESTIGATION_CAPACITY\": 0.01,\n","    \"N_BOOTSTRAP\": 400,\n","    \"BOOTSTRAP_ALPHA\": 0.05,\n","    \"ACCEPTANCE_DELTA\": 0.005,\n","\n","    # --- LightGBM Hyperparameters ---\n","    \"LGB_PARAMS\": {\n","        \"objective\": \"binary\",\n","        \"metric\": \"average_precision\",\n","        \"boosting_type\": \"gbdt\",\n","        \"learning_rate\": 0.03,\n","        \"num_leaves\": 256,\n","        \"max_depth\": -1,\n","        \"min_child_samples\": 50,\n","        # FIX: bagging is inert without bagging_freq > 0.\n","        \"bagging_fraction\": 0.8,\n","        \"bagging_freq\": 1,\n","        \"feature_fraction\": 0.7,\n","        \"seed\": 42,\n","        \"bagging_seed\": 42,\n","        \"feature_fraction_seed\": 42,\n","        \"data_random_seed\": 42,\n","        \"deterministic\": True,\n","        \"force_row_wise\": True,\n","        \"n_jobs\": -1,\n","        \"verbose\": -1,\n","    },\n","    \"NUM_BOOST_ROUND\": 2000,\n","    \"EARLY_STOPPING_ROUNDS\": 50,\n","\n","    # --- File Paths ---\n","    \"CANDIDATE_DATA_DIRS\": [\n","        \"/kaggle/input/competitions/ieee-fraud-detection\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/ieee-fraud-detection\",\n","        \"./data/ieee-fraud-detection\",\n","        \"./data\",\n","        \".\",\n","    ],\n","    \"CANDIDATE_DECISION_PATHS\": [\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/ieee-cis-eda-leakage-audit/artifacts/feature_risk_table.csv\",\n","        \"./artifacts/feature_risk_table.csv\",\n","        \"./artifacts/feature_decisions.csv\",\n","        \"feature_risk_table.csv\",\n","        \"feature_decisions.csv\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/ieee-cis-eda-leakage-audit/feature_risk_table.csv\",\n","        \"/kaggle/input/notebooks/iemanihsan/ieee-cis-eda-leakage-audit/feature_decisions.csv\",\n","    ],\n","    \"OUTPUT_DIR\": \"./artifacts\",\n","}\n","\n","# Columns forbidden in the predictor matrix (target, keys, block/time metadata,\n","# and derived entity strings used only for auditing).\n","TARGET_LEAKAGE_COLUMNS = [\n","    \"isFraud\",\n","    \"TransactionID\",\n","    \"TransactionDT\",\n","    \"elapsed_days\",\n","    \"day_index\",\n","    \"chrono_block\",\n","]\n","AUDIT_ONLY_COLUMNS = [\"uid_card\", \"uid_device\", \"card_first_seen\"]\n","\n","np.random.seed(CONFIG[\"SEED\"])\n","os.makedirs(CONFIG[\"OUTPUT_DIR\"], exist_ok=True)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"b92701ed","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"af04016a-077c-4b02-9680-3a185d7f43c0","_uuid":"fd9c4110-0bf9-4c3a-8380-a9a0877e79b4","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.958334Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.957775Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.996886Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.996195Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":0.044655,"end_time":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.998472+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-30T04:18:50.953817+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# ==============================================================================\n","# 2. Utility Functions\n","# ==============================================================================\n","def sha256_file(path: str) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"Hash file bytes in bounded-memory chunks.\"\"\"\n","    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n","    with open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n","        for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n","            digest.update(chunk)\n","    return digest.hexdigest()\n","\n","\n","script_sha256 = sha256_file(__file__) if \"__file__\" in globals() else None\n","\n","\n","def resolve_path(candidates: list[str], target_file: str | None = None) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"Resolve the first existing directory (or dir/target_file) from candidates.\"\"\"\n","    for path in candidates:\n","        check_path = os.path.join(path, target_file) if target_file else path\n","        if os.path.exists(check_path):\n","            return check_path if target_file else path\n","    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Target {target_file or 'directory'} not found in {candidates}.\")\n","\n","\n","def resolve_first_existing(candidates: list[str]) -> str:\n","    \"\"\"Return the first candidate file path that exists.\"\"\"\n","    for path in candidates:\n","        if os.path.exists(path):\n","            return path\n","    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"No feature-decision ledger found in {candidates}.\")\n","\n","\n","def reduce_memory(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"Downcast numeric columns to shrink the working set without value loss.\"\"\"\n","    before = frame.memory_usage(deep=False).sum() / 1024 ** 2\n","    for col in frame.columns:\n","        kind = frame[col].dtype.kind\n","        if kind == \"i\":\n","            frame[col] = pd.to_numeric(frame[col], downcast=\"integer\")\n","        elif kind == \"f\":\n","            frame[col] = frame[col].astype(np.float32)\n","    after = frame.memory_usage(deep=False).sum() / 1024 ** 2\n","    print(f\"    Memory downcasting: {before:.1f} MB -> {after:.1f} MB \"\n","          f\"({(before - after) / before:.1%} saved)\")\n","    return frame\n","\n","\n","def create_temporal_blocks(\n","    frame: pd.DataFrame,\n","    n_blocks: int,\n","    time_col: str = \"TransactionDT\",\n","    id_col: str = \"TransactionID\",\n",") -> pd.Series:\n","    \"\"\"Assign equal-row-count chronological block labels 1..n_blocks deterministically.\"\"\"\n","    order = frame.sort_values([time_col, id_col], kind=\"mergesort\").index\n","    position = pd.Series(np.arange(len(order)), index=order)\n","    labels = np.minimum((position.values * n_blocks) // len(order), n_blocks - 1) + 1\n","    return pd.Series(labels.astype(np.int16), index=order).reindex(frame.index)\n","\n","\n","def alert_threshold(\n","    amounts: np.ndarray,\n","    c_rev: float = CONFIG[\"C_REVIEW\"],\n","    c_fric: float = CONFIG[\"C_FRICTION\"],\n",") -> np.ndarray:\n","    \"\"\"Bayes-optimal per-transaction alert threshold p* = (C_rev+C_fric)/(Amt+C_fric).\"\"\"\n","    amounts_arr = np.asarray(amounts, dtype=float)\n","    return np.minimum((c_rev + c_fric) / (amounts_arr + c_fric), 1.0)\n","\n","\n","def expected_calibration_error(\n","    y_true: np.ndarray,\n","    y_prob: np.ndarray,\n","    n_bins: int = 20,\n","    strategy: str = \"uniform\",\n",") -> float:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Bin-weighted ECE.\n","\n","    strategy='uniform'  : equal-width bins (standard, but on a ~3.5% prevalence\n","                          problem the [0,0.05) bin swallows ~95% of mass and the\n","                          statistic flatters the model).\n","    strategy='quantile' : equal-frequency bins - a far more discriminating view\n","                          of calibration in the operationally relevant high-score\n","                          region. Report both.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    y_true_arr = np.asarray(y_true, dtype=float)\n","    y_prob_arr = np.clip(np.asarray(y_prob, dtype=float), 0.0, 1.0)\n","    n = len(y_true_arr)\n","    if n == 0:\n","        return float(\"nan\")\n","\n","    if strategy == \"quantile\":\n","        quantiles = np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1)\n","        edges = np.unique(np.quantile(y_prob_arr, quantiles))\n","        if len(edges) < 3:\n","            return expected_calibration_error(y_true_arr, y_prob_arr, n_bins, \"uniform\")\n","        bin_idx = np.clip(np.digitize(y_prob_arr, edges[1:-1], right=False), 0, len(edges) - 2)\n","        n_eff = len(edges) - 1\n","    else:\n","        edges = np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1)\n","        bin_idx = np.clip(np.digitize(y_prob_arr, edges[1:-1], right=False), 0, n_bins - 1)\n","        n_eff = n_bins\n","\n","    total_error = 0.0\n","    for b in range(n_eff):\n","        mask = bin_idx == b\n","        count = int(mask.sum())\n","        if count > 0:\n","            total_error += count * abs(y_prob_arr[mask].mean() - y_true_arr[mask].mean())\n","    return float(total_error / n)\n","\n","\n","def compute_metrics(\n","    y_true: np.ndarray,\n","    y_prob: np.ndarray,\n","    amounts: np.ndarray,\n","    capacity: float = CONFIG[\"INVESTIGATION_CAPACITY\"],\n",") -> dict[str, float]:\n","    \"\"\"Ranking, calibration, triage and economic metrics for a single scored window.\"\"\"\n","    y_true = np.asarray(y_true, dtype=int)\n","    y_prob = np.asarray(y_prob, dtype=float)\n","    amounts = np.asarray(amounts, dtype=float)\n","\n","    # --- Ranking ---\n","    ap = float(average_precision_score(y_true, y_prob))\n","    try:\n","        roc = float(roc_auc_score(y_true, y_prob))\n","    except ValueError:\n","        roc = float(\"nan\")\n","\n","    # --- Probabilistic / calibration ---\n","    p_safe = np.clip(y_prob, 1e-15, 1.0 - 1e-15)\n","    log_loss = float(-np.mean(y_true * np.log(p_safe) + (1 - y_true) * np.log(1.0 - p_safe)))\n","    brier = float(np.mean((y_prob - y_true) ** 2))\n","    ece_u = expected_calibration_error(y_true, y_prob, 20, \"uniform\")\n","    ece_q = expected_calibration_error(y_true, y_prob, 20, \"quantile\")\n","\n","    # --- Operational triage queue (ties broken by amount desc) ---\n","    order = np.lexsort((-amounts, -y_prob))\n","    y_sorted = y_true[order]\n","    n_neg = int((y_sorted == 0).sum())\n","    n_pos = int((y_sorted == 1).sum())\n","    cum_fp = (y_sorted == 0).cumsum()\n","\n","    def recall_at_fpr(target_fpr: float) -> float:\n","        budget = int(np.floor(target_fpr * n_neg))\n","        alerted_pos = int(y_sorted[cum_fp <= budget].sum())\n","        return float(alerted_pos / n_pos) if n_pos > 0 else 0.0\n","\n","    k_cap = max(1, int(np.floor(capacity * len(y_sorted))))\n","    prec_at_cap = float(y_sorted[:k_cap].mean())\n","    rec_at_cap = float(y_sorted[:k_cap].sum() / n_pos) if n_pos > 0 else 0.0\n","\n","    # --- Economic loss ---\n","    def financial_loss(predictions: np.ndarray) -> float:\n","        fn_mask = (y_true == 1) & (predictions == 0)\n","        fp_mask = (y_true == 0) & (predictions == 1)\n","        stolen = amounts[fn_mask].sum()\n","        review = predictions.sum() * CONFIG[\"C_REVIEW\"]\n","        friction = fp_mask.sum() * CONFIG[\"C_FRICTION\"]\n","        return float(stolen + review + friction)\n","\n","    preds_cost_rule = (y_prob > alert_threshold(amounts)).astype(int)\n","    preds_flat_half = (y_prob >= 0.5).astype(int)\n","    loss_no_model = float(amounts[y_true == 1].sum())  # do-nothing reference\n","\n","    return {\n","        \"AP\": ap,\n","        \"ROC_AUC\": roc,\n","        \"LogLoss\": log_loss,\n","        \"Brier\": brier,\n","        \"ECE\": ece_u,\n","        \"ECE_quantile\": ece_q,\n","        \"Recall@0.1%FPR\": recall_at_fpr(0.001),\n","        \"Recall@1.0%FPR\": recall_at_fpr(0.010),\n","        f\"Prec@{capacity:.1%}cap\": prec_at_cap,\n","        f\"Recall@{capacity:.1%}cap\": rec_at_cap,\n","        \"Loss_cost_rule\": financial_loss(preds_cost_rule),\n","        \"Loss_flat_0.5\": financial_loss(preds_flat_half),\n","        \"Loss_no_model\": loss_no_model,\n","        \"AlertRate\": float(preds_cost_rule.mean()),\n","    }\n","\n","\n","def bootstrap_ap_delta(\n","    y_true: np.ndarray,\n","    p_new: np.ndarray,\n","    p_ref: np.ndarray,\n","    n_boot: int = CONFIG[\"N_BOOTSTRAP\"],\n","    alpha: float = CONFIG[\"BOOTSTRAP_ALPHA\"],\n","    seed: int = CONFIG[\"SEED\"],\n",") -> dict[str, float | int]:\n","    \"\"\"Paired bootstrap of AP(p_new) - AP(p_ref) over identical resampled rows.\"\"\"\n","    y_arr = np.asarray(y_true, dtype=int)\n","    p_new_arr = np.asarray(p_new, dtype=float)\n","    p_ref_arr = np.asarray(p_ref, dtype=float)\n","    n = len(y_arr)\n","\n","    observed = float(\n","        average_precision_score(y_arr, p_new_arr) - average_precision_score(y_arr, p_ref_arr)\n","    )\n","    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n","    deltas = np.empty(n_boot, dtype=float)\n","    valid = 0\n","    for _ in range(n_boot):\n","        idx = rng.integers(0, n, size=n)\n","        y_b = y_arr[idx]\n","        if y_b.sum() == 0 or y_b.sum() == n:\n","            continue\n","        deltas[valid] = (\n","            average_precision_score(y_b, p_new_arr[idx])\n","            - average_precision_score(y_b, p_ref_arr[idx])\n","        )\n","        valid += 1\n","\n","    deltas = deltas[:valid]\n","    if valid == 0:\n","        return {\"delta\": observed, \"ci_low\": np.nan, \"ci_high\": np.nan,\n","                \"p_win\": np.nan, \"n_boot\": 0}\n","\n","    ci_low, ci_high = np.percentile(deltas, [100 * alpha / 2, 100 * (1.0 - alpha / 2)])\n","    return {\n","        \"delta\": observed,\n","        \"ci_low\": float(ci_low),\n","        \"ci_high\": float(ci_high),\n","        \"p_win\": float((deltas > 0.0).mean()),\n","        \"n_boot\": int(valid),\n","    }\n","\n","\n","def build_entity_uids(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> tuple[pd.Series, pd.Series]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Registration-anchored entity proxies (audit use only; never fed to the model).\n","    Anchor = day_index - D1, i.e. an approximate account-open date.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    anchor = np.where(\n","        frame[\"D1\"].isna(),\n","        \"na\",\n","        (frame[\"day_index\"] - frame[\"D1\"].fillna(0)).astype(\"int64\").astype(str),\n","    )\n","    uid_card = (\n","        frame[\"card1\"].astype(str) + \"_\"\n","        + frame[\"card2\"].fillna(-1).astype(str) + \"_\"\n","        + frame[\"addr1\"].fillna(-1).astype(str) + \"_\"\n","        + anchor\n","    )\n","    device_info = (frame[\"DeviceInfo\"].fillna(\"no_dev\").astype(str)\n","                   if \"DeviceInfo\" in frame.columns else \"no_dev\")\n","    browser = (frame[\"id_31\"].fillna(\"no_brw\").astype(str)\n","               if \"id_31\" in frame.columns else \"no_brw\")\n","    uid_device = device_info + \"_\" + browser\n","    return pd.Series(uid_card, index=frame.index), pd.Series(uid_device, index=frame.index)\n","\n","\n","def first_seen_flag(entity_series: pd.Series) -> np.ndarray:\n","    \"\"\"True on an entity's first chronological appearance (depends only on the past).\"\"\"\n","    return ~entity_series.duplicated(keep=\"first\").to_numpy()\n","\n","\n","def entity_overlap_rate(frame: pd.DataFrame, train_idx, score_idx, col: str) -> float:\n","    \"\"\"Share of scored rows whose entity was already observed in the training window.\"\"\"\n","    seen = set(frame.loc[train_idx, col].unique())\n","    return float(frame.loc[score_idx, col].isin(seen).mean())\n","\n","\n","def assert_causal(frame: pd.DataFrame, train_idx, score_idx, label: str,\n","                  time_col: str = CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]) -> None:\n","    \"\"\"Hard guarantee that every training row precedes (or ties) every scored row.\"\"\"\n","    if len(train_idx) == 0 or len(score_idx) == 0:\n","        return\n","    train_max = frame.loc[train_idx, time_col].max()\n","    score_min = frame.loc[score_idx, time_col].min()\n","    assert train_max <= score_min, (\n","        f\"CAUSALITY VIOLATION [{label}]: train_max_dt={train_max} > score_min_dt={score_min}\"\n","    )\n","\n","\n","def time_ordered_inner_split(frame: pd.DataFrame, train_idx, frac: float,\n","                             time_col: str = CONFIG[\"TIME_COLUMN\"]):\n","    \"\"\"Split a training index into (fit, stop) where stop is the latest `frac` by time.\"\"\"\n","    train_dt = frame.loc[train_idx, time_col].to_numpy()\n","    threshold = np.quantile(train_dt, 1.0 - frac)\n","    fit_idx = train_idx[train_dt < threshold]\n","    stop_idx = train_idx[train_dt >= threshold]\n","    return fit_idx, stop_idx\n","\n","\n","def train_causal_model(\n","    frame: pd.DataFrame,\n","    train_idx,\n","    features: list[str],\n","    label: str,\n","    fallback_rounds: int,\n","):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Fit LightGBM on `train_idx` using a time-ordered inner split for early stopping.\n","\n","    Returns (model, best_iter, fit_idx, stop_idx, used_early_stopping).\n","    If the inner stopping set is too small or has too few positives, falls back to\n","    a fixed round count rather than early-stopping on noise.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    target = CONFIG[\"TARGET_COLUMN\"]\n","    fit_idx, stop_idx = time_ordered_inner_split(frame, train_idx, CONFIG[\"INNER_VAL_FRAC\"])\n","    n_stop_pos = int(frame.loc[stop_idx, target].sum()) if len(stop_idx) else 0\n","\n","    viable = (len(stop_idx) >= CONFIG[\"MIN_STOP_ROWS\"]\n","              and n_stop_pos >= CONFIG[\"MIN_STOP_POSITIVES\"])\n","\n","    if viable:\n","        fit_data = lgb.Dataset(frame.loc[fit_idx, features],\n","                               label=frame.loc[fit_idx, target].values)\n","        stop_data = lgb.Dataset(frame.loc[stop_idx, features],\n","                                label=frame.loc[stop_idx, target].values,\n","                                reference=fit_data)\n","        model = lgb.train(\n","            CONFIG[\"LGB_PARAMS\"], fit_data,\n","            num_boost_round=CONFIG[\"NUM_BOOST_ROUND\"],\n","            valid_sets=[stop_data],\n","            callbacks=[lgb.early_stopping(CONFIG[\"EARLY_STOPPING_ROUNDS\"], verbose=False)],\n","        )\n","        return model, int(model.best_iteration), fit_idx, stop_idx, True\n","\n","    warnings.warn(\n","        f\"[{label}] inner stopping set too small \"\n","        f\"(rows={len(stop_idx)}, pos={n_stop_pos}); using fixed {fallback_rounds} rounds.\",\n","        RuntimeWarning,\n","    )\n","    fit_data = lgb.Dataset(frame.loc[train_idx, features],\n","                           label=frame.loc[train_idx, target].values)\n","    model = lgb.train(CONFIG[\"LGB_PARAMS\"], fit_data, num_boost_round=fallback_rounds)\n","    return model, int(fallback_rounds), train_idx, np.array([], dtype=int), False\n","\n","\n","def fit_calibrator(model, frame: pd.DataFrame, stop_idx, features: list[str], best_iter: int):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Isotonic calibration fit ONLY on the inner-stopping slice.\n","\n","    The stopping slice is already spent - it cannot be used for reporting - so it\n","    is the only honest calibration surface available without touching the\n","    validation block. Returns None when calibration is disabled or infeasible.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if CONFIG[\"CALIBRATION\"] != \"isotonic\" or len(stop_idx) == 0:\n","        return None\n","    y_stop = frame.loc[stop_idx, CONFIG[\"TARGET_COLUMN\"]].values\n","    if y_stop.sum() < CONFIG[\"MIN_STOP_POSITIVES\"]:\n","        return None\n","    p_stop = model.predict(frame.loc[stop_idx, features], num_iteration=best_iter)\n","    iso = IsotonicRegression(y_min=0.0, y_max=1.0, out_of_bounds=\"clip\")\n","    iso.fit(p_stop, y_stop)\n","    return iso\n","\n","\n","def apply_calibrator(calibrator, probs: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n","    \"\"\"Apply a fitted calibrator; identity passthrough when absent.\"\"\"\n","    if calibrator is None:\n","        return probs\n","    return np.clip(calibrator.predict(probs), 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n","\n","\n","def rounds_from_history(history: dict[int, int], rule: str, floor: int = 10) -> int:\n","    \"\"\"Derive a boosting-round schedule for models that cannot early-stop.\"\"\"\n","    values = list(history.values())\n","    if not values:\n","        return max(floor, 100)\n","    if rule == \"last\":\n","        chosen = values[-1]\n","    elif rule == \"mean\":\n","        chosen = float(np.mean(values))\n","    else:  # median - robust to a single runaway fold\n","        chosen = float(np.median(values))\n","    return max(floor, int(round(chosen)))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"17fdc317","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"ea8137a4-f3e5-46ab-84cc-06b4d2e36a54","_uuid":"f2aeaf0e-4a43-4d01-abff-896881174468","collapsed":false,"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-30T04:18:51.005264Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-30T04:18:51.005036Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-30T04:19:28.508711Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-30T04:19:28.507872Z"},"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"papermill":{"duration":37.509081,"end_time":"2026-09-30T04:19:28.510573+00:00","exception":f